</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Explain why</p>

<p>
<md>(a+b)^n=a^n+b^n</md>
</p>

<p>is generally false.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Explain why</p>

<p>
<md>\sqrt{a+b}
=
\sqrt a+\sqrt b</md>
</p>

<p>is generally false.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Explain why</p>

<p>
<md>\frac1{a+b}
=
\frac1a+\frac1b</md>
</p>

<p>is generally false.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Prove the binomial theorem by induction.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Derive the multinomial theorem from repeated use of the binomial theorem.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Prove the general factorization of <m>a^n-b^n</m>.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Prove the factorization of <m>a^n+b^n</m> for odd <m>n</m>.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Derive the quadratic formula by completing the square.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Prove Vieta's formulas for a quadratic polynomial.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Prove the formula for the sum of the first <m>n</m> squares.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Prove the formula for the sum of the first <m>n</m> cubes.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Derive the finite geometric-series formula algebraically.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
